-- H5b (R-E14 to R-E20): the amend check of a new constitution, a Stack of
-- opcode words in postfix order. The fold reads the last item of the text
-- first, so the text gives the opcodes in reverse order. A word is tag + 16
-- x code (R-E15). The guest has no division: amendCode finds the code with
-- a 24-bit search (R-E39). Check 1 (R-E16) types each fragment on a stack
-- of at most 4 code pairs in a Frag record, and the end must be one pair
-- (13, 19): else 4 AMEND_ILL_TYPED. A code over 8 digits is ill-typed, and
-- amendCap keeps each slot small (R-E42). Check 2 (R-E17): the first 2
-- words are [17, 9] and the last word is 2: else 5 AMEND_NOT_FHE. Check 3
-- (R-E18, R-E43): the decide part is the threshold template with k at least
-- 1, read by a state machine (12 a match, 13 a bad first or second word, 14
